window.docContents[252].resolve({"/Functors___-Monads-and--do--Notation/Syntax/#do-control-structures":{"contents":"There are do elements that correspond to most of Lean's term-level control structures.\nWhen they occur as a step in a do block, they are interpreted as do elements rather than terms.\nEach branch of the control structures is a sequence of do elements, rather than a term, and some of them are more syntactically flexible than their corresponding terms.\n\nConditionalsIn a do block, if statements may omit their else branch.\nOmitting an else branch is equivalent to using pure () as the contents of the branch.\n\nSyntactically, the then branch cannot be omitted.\nFor these cases, unless only executes its body when the condition is false.\nThe do in unless is part of its syntax and does not induce a nested do block.\n\nReverse Conditionals\n\nWhen match is used in a do block, each branch is considered to be part of the same block.\nOtherwise, it is equivalent to the match term.\n\nPattern Matching\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009Functors, Monads and  do -Notation\u0009Syntax\u0009do -Notation","header":"18.3.2.4. Control Structures","id":"/Functors___-Monads-and--do--Notation/Syntax/#do-control-structures"},"/The--grind--tactic/Minimizing--grind--calls/#grind-minimizing-grind-calls":{"contents":"grind only [...] 策略使用受限的定理集合调用 grind，从而可能提升性能。\n可以使用 grind? 方便地构造 grind only 调用；它会自动记录 grind 使用的定理，并建议合适的 grind only。\n\n这些定理通常带有 =、← 或 → 等符号前缀，用来表示\n触发实例化的模式。详情参见关于 E-匹配的章节。\n有些定理可能带有 usr 前缀，表示使用了自定义模式。\n\n","context":"Lean 中文参考手册\u0009grind  策略","header":"16.2. 最小化  grind  调用","id":"/The--grind--tactic/Minimizing--grind--calls/#grind-minimizing-grind-calls"}});